  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759834,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 16 Zhang Mahjong (Sega Mega Drive/Genesis) - Synopsis\n\n16 Zhang Mahjong is a notorious and controversial mahjong game released for the Sega Mega Drive/Genesis, developed by Gamtec. Unlike traditional mahjong, this title gained infamy for being one of several unlicensed games produced that incorporated pornographic imagery and themes. While gameplay fundamentally follows the rules of mahjong – matching tiles to clear your hand and be the first to declare a winning hand – the visual presentation is where the game deviates drastically.\n\nThe game features digitized sprites and backgrounds, often depicting suggestive or explicit scenes, a stark contrast to the typically serene and traditional aesthetic of mahjong. Players engage in a standard four-player mahjong match, strategically discarding and drawing tiles while navigating the distracting and provocative visuals. The game's notoriety stems from its exploitation of the console's capabilities to push boundaries and cater to a niche audience, making it a significant, albeit controversial, piece of Sega's history. It remains a rare and sought-after (or avoided) curiosity for collectors."
    },
